{"ts": "2026-10-04T22:08:26Z", "task_id": "T-004", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 10, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/providers.py", "line": 12, "issue": "_split treats the presence of a separator as sufficient, so a model ending with a colon returns (provider, '') instead of the required (model, model) when rest is empty.", "remediation": "Use the rest value from partition: provider, sep, rest = str(model).partition(':'); if rest: return provider, rest; return model, model."}, {"file": "src/triage/providers.py", "line": 32, "issue": "provider_stats reads model from the top-level event instead of data['model'], which is the layout pinned by the task and will misattribute or drop successful calls in the pre-seeded tests.", "remediation": "Read data = event.get('data') or {}, then model = data.get('model'); skip the event if model is None."}, {"file": "src/triage/providers.py", "line": 53, "issue": "The failed-call loop also uses top-level event['model'] instead of data['model'], causing incorrect provider attribution for errors and timeouts.", "remediation": "Read the same nested data dict for failed events and skip when data or data['model'] is missing."}]}
{"ts": "2026-10-04T22:33:04Z", "task_id": "T-002", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 8, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/latency.py", "line": 65, "issue": "role_latency extracts duration_s and model_role from the top-level event object, but the task specifies that these fields are carried in the event's data payload. The seeded tests use nested data, so valid llm_exchange events are filtered out and role_latency returns {} for non-empty input.", "remediation": "Extract the nested payload first, e.g. data = event.get(\"data\"), then require isinstance(data, dict) before reading duration = data.get(\"duration_s\") and role = data.get(\"model_role\"). Keep the existing numeric/string validation and bool exclusion."}, {"file": "src/triage/latency.py", "line": 122, "issue": "outliers has the same nested-data extraction bug. Because no events are accepted, the function returns [] even when there are at least four valid samples and a max value above the IQR threshold, which is visible in the failing factor=0.0 test.", "remediation": "Use the same event data extraction as role_latency: read event.get(\"data\"), validate it is a dict, then read duration_s and model_role from that dict. Preserve the at-least-four-samples rule, threshold = q3 + factor * iqr, strict max > threshold comparison, and descending duration / ascending role sort."}]}
