{"ts": "2026-10-05T00:56:27Z", "task_id": "T-004", "attempt": 2, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 1, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/providers.py", "line": 11, "issue": "The _split helper returns the full model string as the provider whenever the colon separator is missing (rest is empty), which fails the test at line 60 that expects provider_stats to treat an unprefixed model token (e.g. 'qwen3.8-27b') as the explicit 'default' provider, yielding a fallback_rate/success_rate of 1.0 rather than 0.5.", "remediation": "Treat unprefixed model tokens as the 'default' provider, i.e. make _split return ('default', str(model)) when partition(':') yields an empty rest, while still preserving everything after the first colon as the rest for colound models. Then rerun tests/test_providers.py."}]}
