{"ts": "2026-10-05T01:40:25Z", "task_id": "T-003", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 1, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/failures.py", "line": 137, "issue": "The implementation fails the pre-seeded test `tests/test_failures.py` because `generic_signature` returns an empty string instead of 'SCHEMA'. This indicates the logic for finding the common token across qualifying shapes is incorrect, specifically in how it intersects the token sets.", "remediation": "Review and correct the token intersection logic in `generic_signature`. Ensure that the tokenizer for shape comparison (likely `shape.split('_')`) produces tokens that can be successfully intersected to find the commonality. Verify that the filtering for `count >= 2` and the lower bound on distinct shapes align with the test's expectations for 'SCHEMA' to be the shared root cause."}, {"file": "tests/test_failures.py", "line": 1, "issue": "There is one skipped test in `test_failures.py`. The acceptance criteria state 'no skips'.", "remediation": "Investigate why the test is being skipped (e.g., conditional logic, `pytest.mark.skip`) and either fix the condition or remove the mark so that the test runs. Alternatively, if it was the `test_skipped_signature` test, ensure it is not skipped if the feature is now implemented."}]}
{"ts": "2026-10-05T01:47:28Z", "task_id": "T-003", "attempt": 2, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 1, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/failures.py", "line": 132, "issue": "generic_signature does not exclude the '<N>' placeholder token when computing the intersection of tokens across qualifying shapes. When multiple qualifying shapes share '<N>' (the instance-id placeholder) along with a real token like 'SCHEMA', the intersection has more than one element and the function returns '' instead of the intended common token. The spec's guarantee that 'ties cannot occur' implies only one real token is meant to be common; the placeholder '<N>' is an artefact of normalization, not a meaningful shared token.", "remediation": "Filter out the literal '<N>' token from each token set before computing the intersection. For example, after splitting, use `set(shape.split('_')) - {'<N>'}` for each shape, then compute the intersection. This ensures only real semantic tokens are considered. Verify the fix against the test that expects 'SCHEMA'."}]}
{"ts": "2026-10-05T01:53:24Z", "task_id": "T-003", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 1, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/failures.py", "line": 158, "issue": "tests/test_failures.py:137 failed: generic_signature returned '' but the pre-seeded test expects 'SCHEMA'. The guard `if len(common_tokens) == 1: return ...; return ''` returns '' whenever the intersection of all qualifying shapes' tokens contains more than one token (e.g. when a token like a suffix is common to all qualifying shapes in addition to the expected root-cause token). The spec says to 'return the single token shared by ALL of them' and asserts ties cannot occur in the intended data; returning '' on a multi-token intersection is therefore not the behavior the test encodes.", "remediation": "Instead of returning '' when the intersection has >1 tokens, select the shared token deterministically — e.g. iterate the tokens of the first qualifying shape in left-to-right order and return the first token that is present in every qualifying shape's token set. Then run tests/test_failures.py and confirm the assertion at line 137 passes and the full suite is green."}, {"file": "src/triage/failures.py", "line": 148, "issue": "`tokens.discard('<N>')` excludes the instance-id placeholder from the common-token search. The spec's generic_signature steps say only: consider shapes with count >= 2, split each shape on '_', and return the single token shared by ALL of them — it does not mention excluding '<N>'. This undocumented filter changes the intersection set and can both hide and create apparent ties depending on the data.", "remediation": "Remove the '<N>' discard (or keep it only if the seeded tests demonstrably require it), and re-derive the exact matching behavior from tests/test_failures.py rather than from an assumption about what an 'artefact' token is."}, {"file": "src/triage/failures.py", "line": 135, "issue": "Minor spec deviation in normalise_signature's step 1 (line 34): the spec prescribes `str(signature or \"\").upper()`; the implementation uses `str(signature).upper()` after a None check. Equivalent for str/None/\"\" inputs, but diverges for falsy non-string inputs.", "remediation": "Align exactly with the spec: `s = str(signature or \"\").upper()` so behavior matches the pinned wording for any input the tests might throw at it."}]}
