{"ts": "2026-10-05T02:51:47Z", "task_id": "T-003", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 1, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/triage/failures.py", "line": 115, "issue": "generic_signature implementation intersects distinct qualifying shape tokens as sets, but the requirement states: 'Split each qualifying shape on \"_\" and DISCARD the \"<N>\" placeholder token... Intersect the surviving tokens across all qualifying shapes. Return the single shared token, UPPERCASED, but ONLY when the intersection holds exactly one token'. Using set intersection across all sets can cause common tokens present in subset of shapes to be incorrectly dropped or matched incorrectly if not careful, or more specifically, the test failure AssertionError: assert 'SCHEMA' == '' indicates that a valid single shared token was missed or incorrectly filtered out due to set-based intersection behavior (e.g. order/duplicates or full set intersection logic vs list/sequence intersection).", "remediation": "Review the intersection logic in generic_signature. Ensure that intersection correctly identifies tokens present across all qualifying shapes."}]}
